description:
FILED s537a (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-11), seen while probing #4762's handle slots.  PRE-EXISTING (main 3d524ad7 identical).  A divergence in a discouraged spelling (perlfunc: mixing syswrite with buffered I/O on one handle "can get confused"), so a LOW one -- but the file content differs.

    my $f = "/tmp/x.out";
    open(my $fh, ">", $f) or die; print $fh "p\n"; syswrite($fh, "s\n"); close $fh;
    open($fh, "<", $f) or die; print <$fh>;
      perl 5.40.3:  s / p   (the buffered "p\n" reaches the file at close, after the unbuffered syswrite)
      PCL:          p / s

MECHANISM (not read): PCL's syswrite either flushes the handle's buffer first or writes through the same buffered stream.  perl's pp_syswrite writes to the fd directly (PerlLIO_write) and leaves the PerlIO buffer as it is.  Decide whether to model it at all (a program that depends on it is rare and fragile); if yes, syswrite writes to the fd without flushing.  Probe: scratch/s537a/p/m7.pl in the s537a worktree.
